\pard\qc\b\fs32 PROJECT MEMO\par
\fs24 Monamila Website Launch\par
\pard\sa240\fs22\b0
\b Date:\b0  September 15, 2026\par
\b Status:\b0  Draft for review\par
\b Project owner:\b0  To be confirmed\par
\par
\b Purpose\b0\par
This memo records the current scope of the Monamila customer-facing website and the decisions required to prepare it for launch. It is based on the materials currently present in the project workspace.\par
\par
\b Current deliverable\b0\par
The project includes a responsive, single-page promotional website for Monamila. The existing page presents the brand, a hero message, customer benefits, and an online order form. Its visual direction uses a bold red, orange, and charcoal palette with food photography and a mobile layout.\par
\par
\b Scope in the current draft\b0\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\sa120
\bullet\tab Brand header and promotional hero section.\par
\bullet\tab Benefit cards that communicate product and service value.\par
\bullet\tab Online order interface with customer input fields and product selection.\par
\bullet\tab Responsive styling for desktop and mobile screens.\par
\pard\sa240\par
\b Key observations\b0\par
The page is currently a front-end prototype. The order form and call to action require a confirmed operational destination before public launch, such as a checkout flow, messaging channel, CRM, or delivery platform. Content and operating details, including menu items, pricing, service area, business hours, contact information, and privacy terms, should be verified with the business owner.\par
\par
\b Decisions requested\b0\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\sa120
\bullet\tab Confirm the production domain and hosting owner.\par
\bullet\tab Select the order-routing method and identify the accountable operator.\par
\bullet\tab Approve final copy, photography, menu data, prices, and contact details.\par
\bullet\tab Confirm legal and privacy requirements for collection of customer data.\par
\pard\sa240\par
\b Recommended next steps\b0\par
\pard\li360\fi-180\sa120
\bullet\tab Replace placeholder or externally hosted assets with approved, licensed production assets.\par
\bullet\tab Connect the form to the selected order workflow and validate error handling and confirmation messaging.\par
\bullet\tab Add business details, analytics consent, and privacy information.\par
\bullet\tab Test the final page on current mobile and desktop browsers before release.\par
\pard\sa240\par
\b Success criteria\b0\par
The launch is ready when visitors can understand the offer, select an order path, submit their information securely, receive a clear confirmation, and the business can reliably receive and act on each request.\par
\par
\i This is a working draft. Items marked for confirmation should be completed with the project owner before publication.\i0\par
